=begin
      author: Fizzleworth
        name: fizzport
        game: gemstone
        tags: sorcerer, planar shift, 740, teleport, rune book, chalk
    requires: Lich > 5.14.2
     version: 0.2
        note: Written with assistance from Claude (Anthropic).

  Planar Shift (740) to a pattern in your rune books: ;fizzport icemule

  It finds the destination by name in the rune books in your shiftsack. READ shows each
  pattern's label (e.g. [Icemule Trace, Town Center]) and its rune colour, and the colour
  is the realm. Any part of a label works: ;fizzport hanging gardens

  What it does (gswiki Planar Shift (740)):
    1. Searches each rune book page by page for the label (TURN wraps from page 10 back
       to page 1). Any sorcerer can draw from any book, bonded or not.
    2. Picks the chalk from the realm you're in (the map's location name) and the
       destination's rune colour:
         - same realm                       waxy translucent chalk (cheap)
         - another realm in the same zone   fine crystalline chalk, unless you have 75+
                                            Demonology ranks
         - another zone                     fine crystalline chalk (about 30,000 a trip)
       Cheap chalk on a trip that needs crystalline fails automatically, with backlash.
    3. Book in the right hand, chalk in the left: DRAW SUMMONING CIRCLE, DRAW PATTERN #,
       then puts both away and re-equips your hands.
    4. Waits for 40 mana, PREPAREs 740 and CASTs at the CIRCLE. A backlash leaves the
       circle in place, so it casts again (up to 3 times, while health stays at 60%+).
       A demon coming through the rift stops the script so you can deal with it.
    5. Same realm: a rift opens for 60 seconds and it goes through (GO RIFT). Another
       realm: the cast takes you straight there.

  Shortcuts (anything else is matched against the labels as typed). Fizzleworth's book
  (the blue leather book, bonded) has only the first three so far; SENSE PATTERN with it
  in hand at the others to add them:
    wl, landing        Town Square Central
    ti, illistim       Ta'Illistim, Hanging Gardens
    cys, cysaegir      Cysaegir, Linsandrych Common
    icemule, it        Icemule Trace, Town Center
    sol, solhaven      Solhaven (any label with "Solhaven" in it)
    pinefar            Pinefar Trading Post, Greatroom
    tv, vaalor         Ta'Vaalor, King's Court

  Usage:
    ;fizzport <destination>     e.g. ;fizzport icemule, ;fizzport hanging gardens
    ;fizzport patterns          every pattern in every rune book (reads all the pages, then
                                turns each book back to page 1), saved for ;fizzport list
    ;fizzport list              shortcuts and where each one's pattern is (as of the last
                                ;fizzport patterns), the realm you're in, Demonology ranks
    ;fizzport help              this help and your settings

  Options (after the destination):
    --long       use waxy translucent chalk, whatever fizzport thinks you need
    --crystal    use fine crystalline chalk, whatever fizzport thinks you need
    --tries=N    give up after N casts that backlash (default 3)

  Settings:
    ;vars set shiftsack=<container>   where the rune books and chalk are (falls back to
                                      runestonesack, then infusesack, so the kit works unset)
    ;vars set runebook=<name>         only search this book (e.g. blue.book); default: every
                                      book in the shiftsack

  Verified from Fizzleworth's 10/27 log: READ, TURN and the kit's chalk names. From
  gswiki logs: the DRAW messages and the cross-realm cast. Not seen yet: the same-realm
  rift and GO RIFT from Fizzleworth's own casts. Anything that doesn't match is printed.
=end

module Fizzport
  # === config (edit to taste) ===================================================
  DEFAULT_TRIES      = 3
  # A backlash does mild-to-moderate damage; don't cast again below this
  MIN_HEALTH_PCT     = 60
  # gswiki: below 75 Demonology ranks, other realms (even in the same zone) need crystalline chalk
  CROSS_REALM_RANKS  = 75
  # gswiki: cheap chalk between realms adds 33% failure, minus 1% per 3 ranks over 75
  LONG_CHALK_PENALTY = 33
  BOOK_PAGES         = 10

  # Realms: teleport zone (nil = isolated), rune colour (gswiki Realm and Planar Shift
  # (guide)), and the map `location` names known to be in them. Besides the towns, these
  # come from patterns in Fizzleworth's books (Stone Valley is twilight grey, Gyldemar is
  # sapphire blue, ...). A location that isn't listed means fizzport can't tell which
  # chalk you need; add it here once you know its realm.
  REALMS = {
    "Wehnimer's Landing"          => { zone: 1, color: 'twilight grey',
                                       locations: ["Wehnimer's Landing", "the town of Wehnimer's Landing", 'the Coastal Cliffs', 'Stone Valley'] },
    'Icemule Trace'               => { zone: 1, color: 'frosty white', locations: ['Icemule Trace'] },
    'Solhaven'                    => { zone: 1, color: 'aquamarine',
                                       locations: ['Solhaven', 'the free port of Solhaven', 'the southern part of Solhaven', 'the town of Solhaven'] },
    'Pinefar'                     => { zone: 1, color: 'icy blue', locations: ['the Pinefar Trading Post'] },
    'Icemule Trail-Glacier'       => { zone: 1, color: 'ghostly white', locations: [] },
    'Icemule Trail-Mountain Pass' => { zone: 1, color: 'pearly white', locations: [] },
    'Icemule Trail-Snowy Forest'  => { zone: 1, color: 'bone white', locations: [] },
    'Abandoned Village'           => { zone: 1, color: 'stone grey', locations: [] },
    'Cairnfang'                   => { zone: 1, color: 'ash grey', locations: [] },
    'Northern Caravansary'        => { zone: 1, color: 'slate grey', locations: [] },
    "Ta'Illistim"                 => { zone: 2, color: 'sapphire blue',
                                       locations: ["Ta'Illistim", 'Gyldemar Forest', 'Gyldemar Road', 'the Blighted Forest', 'Sylvarraend Road', 'the Emerald Forest'] },
    "Ta'Vaalor"                   => { zone: 2, color: 'gold-bordered crimson',
                                       locations: ["Ta'Vaalor", "the city of Ta'Vaalor", 'Fearling Pass', 'the Lake of Fear', 'the hamlet of Ravelin'] },
    'Cysaegir'                    => { zone: 2, color: 'verdant green', locations: ['Cysaegir', 'the village of Cysaegir'] },
    "River's Rest"                => { zone: nil, color: 'sky blue', locations: ["River's Rest", "the town of River's Rest"] },
    'Teras Isle'                  => { zone: nil, color: 'molten red', locations: ['Kharam-Dzu', 'the town of Kharam-Dzu', 'the Ruined Temple'] },
    'Zul Logoth'                  => { zone: nil, color: 'coppery brown', locations: ['Zul Logoth'] },
    "Old Ta'Faendryl"             => { zone: nil, color: 'scarlet', locations: ["Old Ta'Faendryl"] },
    'Shadow Valley'               => { zone: nil, color: 'shadowy black', locations: ['the Shadow Valley'] },
  }.freeze

  # Shortcut -> text in the pattern's label
  DESTINATIONS = {
    'wl'       => 'Town Square Central',
    'icemule'  => 'Icemule Trace, Town Center',
    'sol'      => 'Solhaven',
    'pinefar'  => 'Pinefar Trading Post, Greatroom',
    'ti'       => "Ta'Illistim, Hanging Gardens",
    'tv'       => "Ta'Vaalor, King's Court",
    'cysaegir' => 'Cysaegir, Linsandrych Common',
  }.freeze

  ALIASES = {
    'landing' => 'wl', 'it' => 'icemule', 'solhaven' => 'sol',
    'illistim' => 'ti', 'vaalor' => 'tv', 'cys' => 'cysaegir',
  }.freeze

  # Shop names (gswiki): waxy translucent = the cheap chalk (1,000 silvers, 100 trips; LOOK:
  # "very quickly made and of poor quality"), fine crystalline = 30,000 silvers a trip (LOOK:
  # "of superior quality"). The older names are kept in case they turn up.
  # Never mix them in one circle.
  CHALKS = {
    long:    { what: 'waxy translucent chalk', name: /waxy translucent chalk|long translucent chalk|rough stick of white chalk/i },
    crystal: { what: 'fine crystalline chalk', name: /crystalline chalk|stubby translucent chalk/i },
  }.freeze

  # READ, one row per slot (10/27 log):
  #   7. a set of jagged twilight grey "aq-beq-beq" glyphs [Town Square, Small Park]
  #   8.
  PATTERN_ROW = /^\s*(\d{1,2})\.\s+a set of \S+ (.+?) "[^"]*" \S+ \[(.+)\]\s*$/
  LAST_ROW    = /^\s*20\.(?:\s|$)/
  # TURN: "You turn to page 2 of your leather book." / "You flip back to the first page of your book."
  TURNED      = /You turn to page (\d+) of your|You flip back to the first page of your/
  # Hidden from the screen while reading, so 20 rows a page don't flood it. Tested line by
  # line on the text without its tags (10/28: a whole-chunk regex missed every row).
  SQUELCH     = /\A(?:\d{1,2}\.(?:\s.*)?|You turn to page \d+ of your .*|You flip back to the first page of your .*)\z/
  XML_TAG     = /<[^>]*>/
  HOOK        = 'fizzport-squelch'
  # CharSettings key for what ;fizzport patterns last found (a JSON string, so it comes back
  # as plain arrays rather than settings proxies)
  SAVED_KEY   = 'patterns'

  # gswiki player logs (Missoni, Obelin) and Planar Shift (740) messaging
  CIRCLE_DRAWN  = /you outline the shape of a summoning circle/i
  PATTERN_DRAWN = /The circle is prepared|defensive sigil at the center/i
  RIFT_OPENS    = /rift opens/i
  BACKLASH      = /small shadowy rift begins to take form/i
  DEMON         = /implodes upon itself|is standing around, surveying/i
  NO_TELEPORT   = /soft yellow light|peter out/i
  NOT_FOUND     = /could not find what you were referring to|What were you referring to/i
  CAST_END      = /Cast Roundtime|Roundtime|You can't|Cast at what\?|#{NOT_FOUND}/i

  # === helpers ===================================================================
  def self.msg(text)
    respond "[fizzport] #{text}"
  end

  def self.sack
    [UserVars.shiftsack, UserVars.runestonesack, UserVars.infusesack].find { |name| name && !name.strip.empty? }
  end

  # GS4 style names, the way ;vars hold them: "kit", "alchemy kit", "blue.book". The last
  # word is the noun; every other word has to start a word of the item's name.
  def self.matches?(obj, name)
    words = name.to_s.strip.sub(/\Amy\s+/i, '').split(/[\s.]+/)
    return false if words.empty?

    obj.noun.to_s.casecmp?(words.last) && words[0..-2].all? { |word| obj.name.to_s =~ /\b#{Regexp.escape(word)}/i }
  end

  # The shiftsack: worn, or one level down in something worn
  def self.find_container(name)
    top = GameObj.inv.find { |obj| matches?(obj, name) }
    return top if top

    GameObj.inv.each { |container|
      found = container.contents.to_a.find { |obj| matches?(obj, name) }
      return found if found
    }
    nil
  end

  # "look in" forces a fresh listing; GameObj#contents alone can be stale
  def self.contents(container)
    fput "look in ##{container.id}"
    container.contents.to_a
  end

  def self.demonology
    Skills.sorcerous_lore_demonology.to_i
  end

  # "Icemule Trace" / "it" / "hanging gardens" -> text to look for in the labels
  def self.destination_text(words)
    key = words.join.downcase.gsub(/[^a-z]/, '')
    key = ALIASES[key] || key
    DESTINATIONS[key] || words.join(' ')
  end

  def self.current_realm
    location = Room.current&.location.to_s
    REALMS.find { |_realm, info| info[:locations].include?(location) }&.first
  end

  def self.realm_of(color)
    REALMS.find { |_realm, info| info[:color] == color.to_s.downcase }&.first
  end

  def self.extra_failure(ranks)
    [LONG_CHALK_PENALTY - ((ranks - CROSS_REALM_RANKS) / 3), 0].max
  end

  # [chalk kind or nil, why]
  def self.pick_chalk(here, to)
    return [nil, "fizzport doesn't know the realm of the pattern's rune colour"] if to.nil?
    return [nil, "fizzport doesn't know which realm \"#{Room.current&.location || 'this room'}\" is in"] if here.nil?
    return [:long, "same realm (#{to})"] if here == to

    from_zone = REALMS.dig(here, :zone)
    if from_zone.nil? || from_zone != REALMS.dig(to, :zone)
      return [:crystal, "#{here} and #{to} are in different teleport zones"]
    end

    ranks = demonology
    if ranks >= CROSS_REALM_RANKS
      return [:long, "another realm in the same zone; cheap chalk adds #{extra_failure(ranks)}% failure at #{ranks} Demonology ranks"]
    end

    [:crystal, "#{here} and #{to} are different realms, and cheap chalk needs #{CROSS_REALM_RANKS} Demonology ranks for that (you have #{ranks})"]
  end

  # put, not fput: fput would swallow the first response line. Collects until terminator,
  # or until the game goes quiet for `idle` seconds (for text that isn't known yet).
  def self.collect_lines(action, terminator = nil, timeout: 6, idle: 1.0)
    waitrt?
    waitcastrt?
    Script.current.clear
    put action
    lines = []
    deadline = Time.now + timeout
    last_line = nil
    loop do
      line = get?
      if line
        lines << line.strip
        last_line = Time.now
        break if terminator && line =~ terminator
      else
        break if last_line && Time.now - last_line > idle
        break if Time.now > deadline

        sleep 0.1
      end
    end
    lines
  end

  def self.show(lines)
    lines.each { |line| respond "    #{line}" }
  end

  def self.hands
    [GameObj.right_hand, GameObj.left_hand]
  end

  def self.held?(item)
    item && hands.any? { |hand| hand.id == item.id }
  end

  # Gets an item out of the sack by id; returns it in hand, or nil
  def self.take(item)
    line = dothistimeout "get ##{item.id}", 5, /You remove|You get|You grab|You pull|Get what|What were you referring to|could not find/
    return nil unless line =~ /You remove|You get|You grab|You pull/

    20.times {
      held = hands.find { |hand| hand.id == item.id }
      return held if held
      sleep 0.1
    }
    nil
  end

  def self.put_away(item)
    return unless held?(item)

    fput "put ##{item.id} in my #{sack}"
  end

  # Drops rune book rows and TURN lines from what reaches the screen. A dropped line's tags
  # are kept (as Lich's quiet commands do) so stream and style state stays intact.
  def self.squelch_lines(xml)
    kept = xml.lines.map { |line|
      next line unless line.gsub(XML_TAG, '').strip =~ SQUELCH

      tags = line.scan(XML_TAG).join
      tags.empty? ? nil : "#{tags}\n"
    }.compact
    kept.empty? ? nil : kept.join
  end

  def self.squelch(on)
    if on
      DownstreamHook.add(HOOK, proc { |xml| Fizzport.squelch_lines(xml) }, persist: false)
    else
      DownstreamHook.remove(HOOK)
    end
  end

  # The rows of the page the book is open to: [[number, colour, label], ...]
  def self.read_page(book)
    collect_lines("read ##{book.id}", LAST_ROW).map { |line|
      number, color, label = line.match(PATTERN_ROW)&.captures
      number && [number.to_i, color.downcase, label]
    }.compact
  end

  # Turns one page; returns the new page number (TURN wraps from 10 to 1), or nil
  def self.turn(book)
    line = collect_lines("turn ##{book.id}", TURNED).find { |text| text =~ TURNED }
    return nil if line.nil?

    line =~ /page (\d+)/ ? Regexp.last_match(1).to_i : 1
  end

  # The best row for the text: the label itself, else a label containing it. Works on page
  # rows and saved patterns alike, since both end in the label.
  def self.match_row(rows, text)
    wanted = text.downcase
    rows.find { |row| row.last.downcase == wanted } ||
      rows.find { |row| row.last.downcase.include?(wanted) }
  end

  # Reads every page of the book in hand and leaves it open to page 1. Returns
  # [[page, number, colour, label], ...]. READ doesn't say the page number, so the page it
  # was open to comes from the first TURN (nil if no TURN was understood).
  def self.read_book(book)
    first_rows = read_page(book)
    open_page = nil
    page = nil
    rows = []
    (BOOK_PAGES - 1).times {
      page = turn(book)
      break if page.nil?

      open_page ||= page == 1 ? BOOK_PAGES : page - 1
      read_page(book).each { |row| rows << [page, *row] }
    }
    rows += first_rows.map { |row| [open_page, *row] }
    BOOK_PAGES.times {
      break if page.nil? || page == 1

      page = turn(book)
    }
    rows.sort_by { |row_page, number, *| [row_page || 0, number] }
  end

  # [time saved or nil, [[book, page, number, colour, label], ...]]
  def self.saved_patterns
    data = JSON.parse(CharSettings[SAVED_KEY].to_s)
    [Time.at(data['saved'].to_i), data['entries'].to_a]
  rescue JSON::ParserError, TypeError, NoMethodError
    [nil, []]
  end

  def self.save_patterns(entries)
    CharSettings[SAVED_KEY] = JSON.generate({ 'saved' => Time.now.to_i, 'entries' => entries })
  end

  def self.shortcut_names(key)
    ([key] + ALIASES.select { |_word, target| target == key }.keys).join(', ')
  end

  # Shortcut -> the saved pattern it would use, or nil
  def self.shortcut_patterns(entries)
    DESTINATIONS.to_h { |key, text| [key, match_row(entries, text)] }
  end

  def self.where(entry)
    book, page, number = entry
    "#{book}, #{page ? "page #{page}" : 'open page'} ##{number}"
  end

  # Holds each rune book in turn and reads its pages until a label matches. Returns
  # [book, page or nil (the page it was already open to), number, colour, label], with
  # that book in the right hand and open to that page, or nil.
  def self.find_pattern(books, text)
    squelch(true)
    books.each { |book|
      held = take(book)
      next if held.nil?

      fput "swap" if GameObj.left_hand.id == held.id
      page = nil
      BOOK_PAGES.times { |i|
        if i.positive?
          page = turn(held)
          break if page.nil?
        end
        row = match_row(read_page(held), text)
        return [held, page, *row] if row
      }
      put_away(held)
    }
    nil
  ensure
    squelch(false)
  end

  def self.rune_books
    container = find_container(sack)
    if container.nil?
      msg "Can't find your #{sack} (shiftsack) on you."
      return []
    end
    # A rune book still in hand isn't in the sack's listing (10/28: "No rune books in your kit")
    hands.each { |hand| fput "put ##{hand.id} in my #{sack}" if hand.noun == 'book' && hand.name =~ /leather book/i }
    books = contents(container).select { |obj| obj.noun == 'book' }
    UserVars.runebook.to_s.strip.empty? ? books : books.select { |obj| matches?(obj, UserVars.runebook) }
  end

  def self.circle_here?
    (GameObj.loot.to_a + GameObj.room_desc.to_a).any? { |obj| obj.name =~ /summoning circle/i }
  end

  def self.draw(what, success)
    lines = collect_lines("draw #{what}", /Roundtime|#{success.source}|#{NOT_FOUND.source}/i, timeout: 8)
    waitrt?
    return true if lines.any? { |line| line =~ success }

    msg "DRAW #{what.upcase} didn't work. The game said:"
    show(lines)
    false
  end

  def self.wait_for_mana
    cost = Spell[740].mana_cost
    return if checkmana >= cost && Spell[740].affordable?

    msg "Waiting for #{cost} mana (you have #{checkmana})."
    sleep 1 until checkmana >= cost && Spell[740].affordable?
  end

  def self.moved?(rooms_before)
    XMLData.room_count != rooms_before
  end

  def self.wait_to_move(rooms_before, seconds)
    (seconds * 10).times {
      return true if moved?(rooms_before)
      sleep 0.1
    }
    moved?(rooms_before)
  end

  # Returns :moved, :rift, :backlash, :demon, :no_teleport or :unknown, and the lines
  def self.cast_at_circle
    wait_for_mana
    fput "release" unless checkprep == "None"
    dothistimeout "prepare 740", 5, /Your spell is ready|already have/
    rooms_before = XMLData.room_count
    lines = collect_lines("cast circle", CAST_END)
    waitcastrt?

    # A trip between realms may also say the rift opens before it moves you, so check for
    # the move before treating it as a rift to walk through
    rift = lines.any? { |line| line =~ RIFT_OPENS }
    result = if lines.any? { |line| line =~ DEMON } then :demon
             elsif lines.any? { |line| line =~ NO_TELEPORT } then :no_teleport
             elsif lines.any? { |line| line =~ BACKLASH } then :backlash
             elsif wait_to_move(rooms_before, rift ? 2 : 5) then :moved
             elsif rift then :rift
             else :unknown
             end
    [result, lines]
  end

  def self.help
    respond
    respond "fizzport - Planar Shift (740) to a pattern in your rune books."
    respond
    respond "Usage:"
    respond "  ;fizzport <destination>     a shortcut, or any part of a pattern's label"
    respond "                              e.g. ;fizzport icemule, ;fizzport hanging gardens"
    respond "  ;fizzport patterns          every pattern in every rune book (reads all the pages, then"
    respond "                              turns each book back to page 1), saved for ;fizzport list"
    respond "  ;fizzport list              shortcuts and where each one's pattern is, your realm and"
    respond "                              Demonology ranks"
    respond "  ;fizzport help              this help"
    respond
    respond "Options (after the destination):"
    respond "  --long        use #{CHALKS[:long][:what]}, whatever fizzport thinks you need"
    respond "  --crystal     use #{CHALKS[:crystal][:what]}, whatever fizzport thinks you need"
    respond "  --tries=N     give up after N casts that backlash (default #{DEFAULT_TRIES})"
    respond
    respond "Settings:"
    respond "  shiftsack   #{sack || '(not set)'}   rune books and chalk"
    respond "              ;vars set shiftsack=<container> (falls back to runestonesack, then infusesack)"
    respond "  runebook    #{UserVars.runebook.to_s.strip.empty? ? '(every book in the shiftsack)' : UserVars.runebook}"
    respond "              ;vars set runebook=<name> to only search one book (e.g. blue.book)"
    respond
  end

  def self.list
    here = current_realm
    respond
    respond "  You're in #{Room.current&.location || 'an unmapped room'} (realm: #{here || 'unknown'}), " \
            "with #{demonology} Demonology ranks."
    respond
    saved_at, entries = saved_patterns
    found = shortcut_patterns(entries)
    DESTINATIONS.each { |key, label|
      status = if saved_at.nil? then ''
               elsif found[key] then where(found[key])
               else 'no pattern yet'
               end
      respond "  #{shortcut_names(key).ljust(20)} #{label.ljust(33)} #{status}"
    }
    respond
    if saved_at.nil?
      respond "  Run ;fizzport patterns once and this list will show which shortcuts have a pattern."
    else
      others = entries - found.values
      unless others.empty?
        respond "  Other patterns (use any part of the label):"
        others.each { |entry| respond "    #{entry.last.ljust(36)} #{where(entry)}" }
        respond
      end
      respond "  As of ;fizzport patterns on #{saved_at.strftime('%b %-d %H:%M')}. Run it again after a SENSE PATTERN."
    end
    respond "  Anything else is matched against the labels in your rune books."
    respond
  end

  # Reads every page of every rune book, leaves each open to page 1, and saves what it
  # finds for ;fizzport list
  def self.patterns
    books = rune_books
    if books.empty?
      msg "No rune books in your #{sack}."
      return
    end
    empty_hands
    @emptied_hands = true
    entries = []
    squelch(true)
    books.each { |book|
      held = take(book)
      next if held.nil?

      respond
      respond "  #{book.name}:"
      rows = read_book(held)
      respond "    (no patterns)" if rows.empty?
      rows.each { |page, number, color, label|
        respond "    #{page ? "page #{page.to_s.rjust(2)}" : 'open page'}  ##{number.to_s.ljust(3)} #{label.ljust(36)} " \
                "#{color} (#{realm_of(color) || 'unknown realm'})"
        entries << [book.name, page, number, color, label]
      }
      put_away(held)
    }
    squelch(false)
    save_patterns(entries)

    missing = shortcut_patterns(entries).select { |_key, entry| entry.nil? }.keys
    respond
    if missing.empty?
      respond "  Every shortcut has a pattern."
    else
      respond "  Shortcuts with no pattern yet (SENSE PATTERN there with your bonded book in hand):"
      missing.each { |key| respond "    #{shortcut_names(key).ljust(18)} #{DESTINATIONS[key]}" }
    end
    respond "  Saved for ;fizzport list."
    respond
  ensure
    squelch(false)
  end

  # === main ======================================================================
  def self.run(args)
    # Module state survives between runs (Lich re-opens the same module), so reset it
    @cleaned_up = false
    @emptied_hands = false
    @filled_hands = false
    @book = nil
    @chalk = nil

    words = args.reject { |arg| arg.start_with?('--') }
    tries = (args.find { |arg| arg =~ /^--tries=\d+$/ }&.split('=')&.last || DEFAULT_TRIES).to_i
    forced = (:long if args.include?('--long')) || (:crystal if args.include?('--crystal'))

    if words.empty? || words.first =~ /^(help|\?)$/i
      help
      exit
    elsif words.first =~ /^list$/i
      list
      exit
    end

    if sack.nil?
      msg "Set the container with your rune books and chalk first: ;vars set shiftsack=<container name>"
      exit
    end

    # before_dying, not ensure: on ;kill the script's thread dies first and fput from its
    # ensure fails; before_dying runs after
    before_dying { Fizzport.cleanup }

    if words.first =~ /^patterns?$/i
      patterns
      exit
    end

    unless Spell[740].known?
      msg "You don't know Planar Shift (740)."
      exit
    end
    if circle_here?
      msg "There's already a summoning circle here. RUB CIRCLE to erase it (if it's yours), or move, then try again."
      exit
    end

    text = destination_text(words)
    books = rune_books
    if books.empty?
      msg "No rune books in your #{sack}."
      exit
    end

    empty_hands
    @emptied_hands = true
    @book, page, number, color, label = find_pattern(books, text)
    if @book.nil?
      msg "No pattern labelled \"#{text}\" in your rune books (;fizzport patterns lists them)."
      exit
    end
    if XMLData.room_title.to_s.include?("[#{label}]")
      msg "You're already at #{label}."
      exit
    end

    to = realm_of(color)
    here = current_realm
    chalk_kind, why = pick_chalk(here, to)
    if forced
      chalk_kind = forced
      why = "you asked for #{CHALKS[forced][:what]}"
    elsif chalk_kind.nil?
      msg "#{why}, so it can't tell which chalk #{label} (#{color}) needs. Run it again with --long " \
          "(same realm) or --crystal (another realm or zone)."
      exit
    end

    msg "#{label}: #{@book.name}, #{page ? "page #{page}" : 'the page it was open to'}, pattern #{number} " \
        "(#{color}, #{to || 'unknown realm'})."
    msg "Using #{CHALKS[chalk_kind][:what]}: #{why}."

    chalk = contents(find_container(sack)).find { |obj| obj.name =~ CHALKS[chalk_kind][:name] }
    @chalk = chalk && take(chalk)
    if @chalk.nil?
      msg "No #{CHALKS[chalk_kind][:what]} in your #{sack}."
      exit
    end

    exit unless draw('summoning circle', CIRCLE_DRAWN)
    exit unless draw("pattern #{number}", PATTERN_DRAWN)

    # gswiki: the book and chalk aren't needed once the circle is drawn
    put_away(@chalk)
    put_away(@book)
    fill_hands
    @filled_hands = true

    casts = 0
    loop do
      casts += 1
      result, lines = cast_at_circle
      case result
      when :moved
        msg "Arrived: #{XMLData.room_title}"
        return
      when :rift
        rooms_before = XMLData.room_count
        fput "go rift"
        if wait_to_move(rooms_before, 5)
          msg "Arrived: #{XMLData.room_title}"
        else
          msg "The rift opened but GO RIFT didn't move you. It stays open for 60 seconds."
        end
        return
      when :demon
        msg "!!! A DEMON CAME THROUGH THE RIFT !!! Fight it or run. Stopping."
        return
      when :no_teleport
        msg "This room blocks teleporting (the runes glowed yellow and faded). Move somewhere else; RUB CIRCLE to erase it."
        return
      when :backlash
        msg "Backlash on cast #{casts}. The circle is still here."
        sleep 0.5 while checkstunned
        waitrt?
        if casts >= tries
          msg "#{casts} backlashes. Stopping; the circle is still here for another try."
          return
        end
        if percenthealth < MIN_HEALTH_PCT
          msg "Health is #{percenthealth}%. Stopping until you heal; the circle is still here."
          return
        end
      else
        msg "Cast #{casts} didn't open a rift or move you. The game said:"
        show(lines)
        return
      end
    end
  end

  # Puts the book and chalk back if they're still in hand and re-equips what was in hand
  def self.cleanup
    return if @cleaned_up

    @cleaned_up = true
    squelch(false)
    fput "release" unless checkprep == "None"
    put_away(@chalk)
    put_away(@book)
    hands.each { |hand| fput "put ##{hand.id} in my #{sack}" if hand.noun == 'book' || hand.name =~ /chalk/i }
    fill_hands if @emptied_hands && !@filled_hands
  end
end

Fizzport.run(Script.current.vars[1..] || [])
